course: dictionary
lesson: 4311
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. Groom is one of them. The sentence around the word tells you which meaning is right. «At weddings the bride and groom make their promises» points to a man on his wedding day.
explain: «Monkeys groom each other, picking out dirt, dead skin and bugs.» Picking out dirt is the clue. Here groom means to brush and clean an animal's fur or coat.
explain: Groom can also be a doing word, a verb. «Well-groomed» means neat and tidy. To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have found the right one.
fact: Groom can be a noun (a thing or a person) or a verb (an action word).
fact: «Groom» can mean a man on his wedding day, also called the bridegroom.
fact: A groom is a person whose job is to look after horses: feeding, brushing and cleaning them.
fact: To groom an animal means to brush and clean its fur or coat. Monkeys groom each other to keep their fur clean and to make friends.
fact: Sometimes grooming means an adult wrongly making friends with a child to trick and harm them. If anyone online or nearby asks you for secrets, gifts or to meet, tell a trusted adult straight away.
exercise: «Next door the chimpanzees sit grooming each other.» What does grooming mean here? | Playing a loud game | Cooking a meal | Shouting at the neighbours | *Cleaning each other's fur and skin
exercise: «The bride and groom made their promises.» What does groom mean here? | To make yourself neat | A person who looks after horses | *A man on his wedding day | To brush an animal's coat
exercise: «She was groomed to be captain.» What does groomed mean? | Brushed clean | Married | Trapped | *Prepared for a job
test: «Grooming cleans the coat and lets the rider check for cuts.» Which meaning of groom is this? | Tidying a bedroom | Making a stable tidy | A man on his wedding day | *Brushing and cleaning an animal's coat
test: Someone online asks you to keep a secret from your family. What should you do? | Keep the secret, because they are your friend | Wait a week and say nothing | Send them a photo | *Tell a trusted adult straight away
exam: Which sentence uses groom as a verb (an action word)? | «The bride and groom danced all night.» | «The groom fed the horses at dawn.» | *«Monkeys groom each other to keep their fur clean.» | «The groom wore a smart blue suit.»
